1	# Compact single-section form with progressive disclosure and live-updating label
2	
3	A single `FormLayout` that collects several related fields compactly, conditionally reveals a dependent field when a specific option is selected, and keeps a summary label in sync with the user's choices at all times. The defining patterns are: progressive disclosure (a hidden field becomes visible only when a triggering option is chosen), dynamic helper text on a `RadioButtonGroup` that reflects the consequence of each selection, and a live-computed `Span` that recalculates whenever any contributing field changes.
4	
5	## Design principles demonstrated
6	
7	* Keep a single logical group in one `FormLayout` when all fields belong to one task
8	* Use progressive disclosure — only reveal fields when they become relevant
9	* Reveal dependent fields inline, immediately below the control that triggers them
10	* Use `CheckboxGroup` for multi-select options, `RadioButtonGroup` for mutually exclusive choices
11	* Orient both groups horizontally to reduce vertical scroll
12	* Use dynamic helper text to reinforce the consequence of a choice in real time
13	* Preselect a sensible default for the most common option
14	* Keep a live-computed summary label so the user always sees the current state before submitting
15	* Use an icon prefix to add visual context to a field without adding a separate label
16	* Wrap asymmetric fields (one wide + one or more narrow) in a `HorizontalLayout` to control proportions
17	* Constrain form width with `setMinWidth` / `setMaxWidth` for comfortable reading at large viewports
18	* Use `FormRow` to place two equal fields side by side
19	
